# MERADGEN workspace

A C++ port of MERADGEN, a FORTRAN 77 Møller-scattering radiative-correction
event generator. The downstream consumer is the Geant4 application MolPol.

## Layout

| Path | Role |
|---|---|
| `meradgen-fortran/` | Verified-pristine upstream FORTRAN. The reference. |
| `meradgen10.tar` | Original upstream tarball the reference was extracted from. |
| `meradgen-cpp/` | Parity C++. FORTRAN literals, float `atan2`, `sngl`. |
| `meradgen-cpp-final/` | Production library for MolPol/Geant4. |
| `comparison-autoreport/` | Parameterized memo + parity `harness/`. |
| `tests/` | Formal tests of production C++. Not started. |
| `MolPolMeradgenOLD/` | Prior glue. Local-only (gitignored). |
| `WORK_NOTES_STATUS.md` | Live open issues and which tree is authoritative. |
| `WORK_NOTES_DEVELOPMENT.md` | Append-only notebook of discoveries. |
| `WORK_NOTES_PARITY.md` | Checklist for matching FORTRAN. |
| `WORK_NOTES_TODO.md` | Production punch list. |
| `WORK_NOTES_MERADGEN_TYPOS.md` | Upstream typos fixed only in production. |

## The governing invariant

The C++ port exists to **reproduce** the FORTRAN, not to improve on it.
Cleaner algebra and better constants are never incidental — each is a
deliberate, recorded decision. Upstream oddities stay in the parity tree
unless a decision says otherwise.

## Before proposing numerical changes

Read `WORK_NOTES_STATUS.md`. Do not rewrite `WORK_NOTES_DEVELOPMENT.md`;
propose new entries and wait for approval.

## Removed trees

`validation_checks/`, `quick-check/`, and `validation_checks_new/` (campaign
archive) were removed. Parity drivers live under
`comparison-autoreport/harness/`. `MolPolMeradgenOLD/` is gitignored.
